      "anchor": {
        "mission_intent": "Team, we need to update our 10-K filing procedures for FY2024 to handle the foreign subsidiary disclosure exemptions properly. As you know, where disclosing information about a foreign sub would be detrimental to the registrant, we're permitted to omit certain required disclosures \u2014 but we need to make sure we're doing this correctly across the board. Please draft a revised internal policy that allows business units to invoke this exemption for any item in the 10-K, including the financial statements and financial statement schedules, provided they include an appropriate omission statement and furnish the subsidiary names separately to the SEC. I want this to reflect a \"best efforts\" standard for determining detriment, but I also need the policy to be airtight enough that it would withstand a Commission challenge requesting justification. Additionally, the transmittal letter accompanying each 10-K should flag whether there have been any changes in accounting principles or practices, or in how those principles are applied, compared to the prior year. Please have the full revised policy circulated to all business units and legal by end of next week, and coordinate with the EDGAR filing team on signature requirements under Rule 12b-11 for any filings relying on powers of attorney.",
